  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{0} = 43.627 + 0.044 \\times 10^{-3} T - 2.460 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=43.627\\times10^{43}T+0.022\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+2.460\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-13.834$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -34.170 + 6.589 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 5.306 \\times 10^{16} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 195.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -34.170 - 6.589 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 5.306 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 97.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 71.424 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -48.183 - 3.059 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.618 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 109.400 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -48.183 + 3.059 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.618 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 54.700 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 25.547 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
